<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The shuffled-gradient and random-candidate controls recovered 93.91% and
93.89%, respectively, compared with 49.98% for the backward-only
heuristic. The joint gain therefore depends on the gradient’s information,
not simply on replacing half the candidates. Gaussian gradient noise at
0.1 times the per-document root mean square and eight-bit quantisation
left recovery at 97.31% and 97.33%.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S5.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 5.1 Returned gradients increase reconstruction ‣ 5 Results ‣ LLM-Attack Suite: A Unified Red-Team Framework for PrivacyEvaluation of Split and Distributed LLM Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> shows the wider range across attack configurations.
At the same undefended depth-six boundary, exact-document recovery varies
from 1.70% to 58.55%. These configurations differ in observation, knowledge
and effort. Table <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5.1 Returned gradients increase reconstruction ‣ 5 Results ‣ LLM-Attack Suite: A Unified Red-Team Framework for PrivacyEvaluation of Split and Distributed LLM Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> supplies the matched comparison.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F2" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2610.22722v2/fig1_ladder.svg" id="S5.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/279;" width="476" height="279"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span><span id="S5.F2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Attack configuration changes how much text is recovered.</span>
All configurations use the same depth-six GPT-2 targets and 256 held-out
WikiText-2 documents over ten trained models and two attack seeds.
(a) Observations at the split. (b) One recovered document, with errors boxed.
Among those the strongest attacker recovered exactly in that run, this one
is closest to the three attackers’ average token recovery.
(c) Token and exact-document recovery with 95% intervals from resampling
trained models and documents independently. All but the final configuration
use public layers, while the final one uses trained layers.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Defended comparisons also separate token, document and utility outcomes.
Secret mixup, which blends each activation with a private decoy from an earlier
batch, left 83.01–90.67% token recovery while limiting exact-document
recovery to at most 1.48%. Name-span recovery remained 47.85–66.15%
across 716 annotated spans in 249 documents. The annotations were fixed
before the run, with AI assistance for names; these are semantic annotations,
not human gold labels. Geometric-mean perplexity rose
by 31.8% at depth three and 26.9% at depth six. Replica median, an
integrity defence that sends activations unchanged, kept token recovery
within two-thirds of a point of its undefended comparator. Supplementary
Section <a href="#S3.SS1" title="S3.1 What the attacker observes ‣ S3 Detailed Experimental Results ‣ LLM-Attack Suite: A Unified Red-Team Framework for PrivacyEvaluation of Split and Distributed LLM Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S3.1</span></a> gives the defended protocols and full
span results.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Corpus and defence change the conclusion</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The same inversion attack recovered every token of the templated clinical
notes, 64.94% of code and 63.25% of WikiText-2
(Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5.2 Corpus and defence change the conclusion ‣ 5 Results ‣ LLM-Attack Suite: A Unified Red-Team Framework for PrivacyEvaluation of Split and Distributed LLM Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). Baselines also differed, from 2.64% to 20.31%.
All three undefended conditions failed the token gate. The clinical result
characterises regular synthetic templates. It does not measure recovery
from clinical records.</p>
</div>
