<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We also ran paired comparisons against two defences, secret
mixup and replica median. Each defended model is trained separately with its
defence in place.
<em id="S3.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Secret mixup</em> blends each activation with a real activation from an
earlier training batch, three parts true to one part decoy. The client
keeps secret which earlier activation it mixed in, and it corrects the
returned gradient for the decoy. Under it, token recovery ranged from
83.01% to 90.67% and whole-document recovery reached at most 1.48%, while
separate utility measurements showed the geometric-mean perplexity rise by
31.8% at depth three and 26.9% at depth six. We also scored annotated
<em id="S3.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">spans</em>, the stretches of text that hold a name, a number or an
identifier. Under secret mixup the attacker recovered 47.85–66.15% of
name spans (716 spans in 249 documents), 93.94–96.50% of number spans
(297 spans in 142 documents) and 90–100% of identifier spans (two spans
in two documents), against 67.36–97.44% of name spans without the
defence. The annotations were fixed before the run, with names marked with
AI assistance. These semantic annotations are not human gold labels.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Replica median</em> runs three copies of the server’s layers and takes
the median of their outputs, number by number. It protects the integrity
of the server’s result and sends the activation unchanged, so token
recovery stayed within two-thirds of a point of the undefended attack.
Whole-document recovery still moved by up to 7.7 points in the most
affected setting (public copy, depth three, SipIt at 128 steps, from
43.77% to 36.11%). The defended model is a separate training run, with
three slightly perturbed server copies, so its client layers end slightly
different, and because one wrong token spoils a document, small changes
per token move many whole documents.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The prespecified contrast and all secondary intervals are recorded in
<a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/Setloop/LLM-Attack-Suite/blob/v2.0/v3-campaign/review/contrasts.json" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href"><span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink">v3-campaign/review/contrasts.json</span></a>;
