<div id="S3.SS8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS8.p3.1" class="ltx_p">There were no failures or skips. In the dependence stress case, increasing
perfectly correlated document columns
from two to 500 preserved the interval <math id="S3.SS8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> rather than treating the
copies as independent evidence. The BiSR prediction process produced
byte-identical outputs after its scorer-only truth file changed and rejected
a manifest that supplied that truth to the predictor. These results establish
conformance of the selected measurement procedures on their fixed cases.
They complement the external-reference comparison in
Section <a href="#S3.SS4" title="S3.4 Which published attack the evaluator runs ‣ S3 Detailed Experimental Results ‣ LLM-Attack Suite: A Unified Red-Team Framework for PrivacyEvaluation of Split and Distributed LLM Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S3.4</span></a> and the real-model leakage measurements.</p>
</div>
