<section id="S4a" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">S4 </span>Release and Reproduction</h2>

<div id="S4a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4a.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The main experiment ran as sixteen deterministic slices across two machines,
merged with hash verification, so that depth is never tied to one host;
the merge checks that every prediction record and every log verifies and
that the runs together equal the planned set. Its 860 binary-tier
references are hash-verified against the pinned baseline release, with no
missing or mismatched files. The Hugging Face dataset at
<a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/Setloop/LLM-Attack-Suite" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/datasets/Setloop/LLM-Attack-Suite</a> holds the predictions, logs and captures of the main
experiment, the domain, horizon and clustered analyses, the two distinct
agentic packages, the positive controls, and the code, protocols and inputs.
Tag <span id="S4a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">v2.0</span> collects the retained campaign evidence, the revised manuscript
and the measurement-validation records identified below. It reuses the
unchanged scientific evidence from v1.0 and changes branding and paper
packaging only, with no new experiments or runtime changes. Experimental files
retain their original hashes; source snapshots preserve the code needed for
reproduction independently of the former Git history.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4a.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4a.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The manuscript, reviewed 64-module taxonomy and released code snapshot
have distinct roles; Table <a href="#S4.T13" title="Table S13 ‣ S4 Release and Reproduction ‣ LLM-Attack Suite: A Unified Red-Team Framework for PrivacyEvaluation of Split and Distributed LLM Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S13</span></a> records each
identifier and scope. The GitHub remote
<a href="https://github.com/setloop-io/LLM-Attack-Suite/tree/v2.0" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/setloop-io/LLM-Attack-Suite/tree/v2.0</a> is the canonical
source release, and the tagged Hugging Face release is the reproducibility artifact.
The released command-line tool offers self-test, module listing, scorecard,
coverage and profile reports, and the synthetic tier needs no deep-learning
stack. Tables <a href="#S4.T12" title="Table S12 ‣ S4 Release and Reproduction ‣ LLM-Attack Suite: A Unified Red-Team Framework for PrivacyEvaluation of Split and Distributed LLM Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S12</span></a> and <a href="#S4.T13" title="Table S13 ‣ S4 Release and Reproduction ‣ LLM-Attack Suite: A Unified Red-Team Framework for PrivacyEvaluation of Split and Distributed LLM Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S13</span></a> give the principal
release locations and identifiers.</p>
</div>
