<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Measurement-validation supplement.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The additional validation run in
Section <a href="#S3.SS8" title="S3.8 Validation of the evaluation methodology ‣ S3 Detailed Experimental Results ‣ LLM-Attack Suite: A Unified Red-Team Framework for PrivacyEvaluation of Split and Distributed LLM Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S3.8</span></a> is supplied in
<a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/Setloop/LLM-Attack-Suite/tree/v2.0/validation/measurement-20261001" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href"><span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink">validation/measurement-20261001/</span></a>
within release <span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">v2.0</span>, unchanged from v1.0. The corresponding path in the maintained
source repository is <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_ref_self">validation/measurement-20261001/</span>. Its original
selection, expected outcomes and per-case observations remain in
<span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_ref_self">selection.json</span> and <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_ref_self">run/results.json</span>; the original
<span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_ref_self">MANIFEST.sha256</span> is preserved unchanged. The package also contains
<span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_ref_self">source-snapshot.tar.gz</span>, which matches all 123 retained source-file
hashes, and <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_ref_self">reproduce_from_snapshot.py</span>, which reproduces the frozen
selection without Git history. Added packaging files have separate digests in
<span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_ref_self">SNAPSHOT.sha256</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5a" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">S5 </span>Names in the Released Files</h2>

<div id="S5a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5a.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The application is named LLM-Attack Suite. Its earlier name,
LLM-Attacker, may remain in software identifiers, paths and historical
release metadata. These retained identifiers refer to this suite, not
the autonomous-driving framework of Mei et al. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>.
The naming change does not alter the frozen experimental evidence.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5a.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5a.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The released files use internal names for the experiments and attacks. The
main experiment is the
<em id="S5a.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">v3</em> campaign, and the adapted comparison is the <em id="S5a.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">v4</em> adaptation.
The joint attack is <span id="S5a.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">joint_true_k32</span>, the activation-only attack is
<span id="S5a.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">forward_k32</span>, the shuffled-gradient and random-candidate controls
are <span id="S5a.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">joint_shuffled_k32</span> and <span id="S5a.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">joint_random_k32</span>, the
backward-only heuristic is <span id="S5a.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">backward</span>, and SipIt with 32, 64 and 128
steps per token is <span id="S5a.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sipit_steps32</span>, <span id="S5a.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sipit_steps64</span> and
<span id="S5a.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sipit_steps128</span>. The BiSR implementation
check is the <em id="S5a.p2.1.11" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">C-A</em> route, and the inverter and its refinement are
<em id="S5a.p2.1.12" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">SIP</em> and <em id="S5a.p2.1.13" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">bf</em>. The pass rule’s current version is
<span id="S5a.p2.1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">frozen-gate.v2</span> and the scorecard policy is
<span id="S5a.p2.1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">scorecard-policy.v3</span>. The benchmark profiles are
<span id="S5a.p2.1.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">benchmark.split-privacy.v2</span>,
<span id="S5a.p2.1.17" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">benchmark.split-integrity-availability.v1</span>,
<span id="S5a.p2.1.18" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">benchmark.genai-app.v1</span> and <span id="S5a.p2.1.19" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">benchmark.agentic.v12</span>, and the
observation points of Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure S2 ‣ S1 Threat Model and Setup ‣ LLM-Attack Suite: A Unified Red-Team Framework for PrivacyEvaluation of Split and Distributed LLM Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S2</span></a> and Table <a href="#S1.T1" title="Table S1 ‣ S1 Threat Model and Setup ‣ LLM-Attack Suite: A Unified Red-Team Framework for PrivacyEvaluation of Split and Distributed LLM Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S1</span></a> are S1–S14.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6a" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">S6 </span>Full Module List and Full-Precision Numbers</h2>

<section id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Attack modules and record.</h4>

<div id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each run writes one JSON record with the fields <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">schema</span>,
<span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">config</span>, <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">threat_model</span>, <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">provenance</span>,
<span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">results</span> and <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">summary</span>. The coverage report marks each threat
as COVERED, PARTIAL, UNMEASURED or OUT_OF_SCOPE. The benchmark profiles
group the threats: <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">benchmark.split-privacy.v2</span> covers the split
privacy families with tenant isolation, telemetry leakage and the router
channel; <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">benchmark.split-integrity-availability.v1</span> covers protocol
integrity, malicious client and server, poisoning, resource exhaustion, key
abuse and supply chain; <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">benchmark.genai-app.v1</span> covers the OWASP LLM
list; and <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">benchmark.agentic.v12</span> covers the OWASP agentic list and is
out of scope by default. Table <a href="#S6.T14" title="Table S14 ‣ Attack modules and record. ‣ S6 Full Module List and Full-Precision Numbers ‣ LLM-Attack Suite: A Unified Red-Team Framework for PrivacyEvaluation of Split and Distributed LLM Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S14</span></a> lists the 64 modules by
family; the count is exact at the reviewed revision
<span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">submission-candidate-20260922-r2</span>.</p>
</div>
