<section id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Validation tiers and artifacts.</h4>

<div id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S6.T15" title="Table S15 ‣ Validation tiers and artifacts. ‣ S6 Full Module List and Full-Precision Numbers ‣ LLM-Attack Suite: A Unified Red-Team Framework for PrivacyEvaluation of Split and Distributed LLM Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S15</span></a> accounts for every module at the reviewed
64-module revision and assigns its primary evidence class. <em id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Reproduced</em>
records agreement with an external reference on fixed inputs; <em id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">adapted</em>
records a prior attack family implemented under a declared local contract;
<em id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">qualification-tested</em> records a framework-native module run against a
real model, capture or deployment; <em id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">synthetic</em> records qualification on a
deterministic fixture or simulator; and <em id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">unmeasured/helper</em> identifies
orchestration components whose outputs are provenance and budget records.
Status <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Q-REAL</span> denotes real-model or deployment qualification,
<span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Q-SYN</span> synthetic qualification, <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PARTIAL</span> a mixed evidence
tier, <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">UNMEAS</span> a pending target measurement, and <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">HELPER</span>
orchestration support. Protected and null outcomes qualify a module when they
match their controls. Deployment claims require <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Q-REAL</span> evidence under
the corresponding deployment protocol.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Artifact keys keep the matrix readable. <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PA/V3</span> is the shared Paper A/B
<span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_ref_self">v3-campaign/</span>; <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PB/PC</span>, <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PB/DS</span>, <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PB/LH</span>,
<span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PB/WB</span>, <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PB/BC</span>, <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PB/BA</span> and <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PB/AG</span> are the
current release’s positive controls, domain, horizon, white-box, BiSR
conformance, BiSR adaptation and agentic packages listed in
Table <a href="#S4.T12" title="Table S12 ‣ S4 Release and Reproduction ‣ LLM-Attack Suite: A Unified Red-Team Framework for PrivacyEvaluation of Split and Distributed LLM Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S12</span></a>. <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">P1/AUD</span> and <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">P1/E8--ER</span> refer to the
frozen audit and historical qualification artifacts indexed by the Paper 1
release <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>. <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">T/name</span> is the named
module’s deterministic fixture and self-test in the reviewed code tag. The
artifact column names evidence, not merely the source file that registers the
module.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T15" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table S15: </span><span id="S6.T15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Validation matrix for all 64 reviewed modules.</span> “Expected”
is the direction fixed by the module contract; “observed” is the retained
qualification outcome, including negative and protected results. Qualification
tests whether the implementation behaves as specified; tier and status
distinguish real-target, synthetic and helper evidence.</figcaption>
<table id="S6.T15.6" class="ltx_tabular">
