<section id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Full-precision numbers.</h4>

<div id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The main experiment’s primary difference is <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.1714" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3.1714</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.1714</annotation></semantics></math> percentage points; the
Wilson multiplier is <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=2.5391848136513127" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.5391848136513127</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=2.5391848136513127</annotation></semantics></math>; the bootstrap uses 100,000
replicates with seed 93281. The domain-battery floors round to 3.911, 2.603
and 2.342 percentage points. The main experiment used 336.1 hours of summed
online attack time and wrote 17 hash-chained logs. The validated white-box
runs each record 128 optimisation steps at learning rate 0.05, a victim
learning rate of <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, 64 training steps, 32 calibration and 32
attacked sequences, 1,024 scored positions, 131,072 token positions in
each direction and 51,463,168 vocabulary comparisons in readout, with
1,223.24 seconds of attack time over the 198 stable runs and 617.16 seconds
over the 99 co-trained runs. The BiSR implementation check trained six
inverters for 20 epochs on 112 auxiliary articles (15,604 windows), ran 24
prediction settings (6,144 document-engine runs) and used an equivalence
interval of <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-0.01,0.01)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0.01</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-0.01,0.01)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=2.919985580355516" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.919985580355516</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=2.919985580355516</annotation></semantics></math>; every one of the
32 comparisons gave the interval <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,0]</annotation></semantics></math>, which describes the agreement on
these fixed documents. The adapted comparison ran two attack seeds (17, 29) in 80 joint
executions, for 160 scored runs and 20,480 document executions, reused 240
control runs, trained four GRU inverters, one per depth and attack seed, for
twenty epochs, applied 32
gradient-matching and 800 activation-matching steps, multiplied the stored
gradients by 256 to convert the loss normalisation to a per-document mean,
and used 29.70 hours of prediction time and 0.58 hours of preparation.
Independent audits on two CPU hosts of the 500-step extension verified all
13 execution journals and 12,443 raw files. The live-planner canaries and
full run used 234.79 seconds of worker wall time.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Synthetic order-and-decoy battery.</h4>

<div id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Some defences shuffle the order of the activations and add decoy rows. A
synthetic battery, with data generated by the framework, ran the matching
module against such data for three seeds. In its six matching reports,
the highest excess of order recovery over chance ranged from 0.52 to 5.21
points. The matching module is a local supervised baseline, and the battery
shows that the framework scores the order of the
rows separately from their tokens.</p>
</div>
